        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 120523,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Conosci già gli oggetti JS. Ora scopriamo cos'è JSON.</p><p>JSON sta per <strong>JavaScript Object Notation</strong>. Possiamo usare questo formato di dati per scambiare dati tra applicazioni web e server.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "JSON quote",
            "id": 120529,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>JSON sembra una versione <em>serializzata</em> di un normale oggetto JS.</p><p>Possiamo creare <code>jsonVariable</code> come un normale oggetto <code>{}</code>, ma racchiuso tra apici singoli <code>'</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" jsonVariable = \" /><text value=\"'{}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"21\" endIndex=\"22\" /><option startIndex=\"22\" endIndex=\"23\" /><option startIndex=\"23\" endIndex=\"24\" /><option startIndex=\"24\" endIndex=\"25\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>'</code>, seguito da <code>{</code> e poi <code>}</code>, <code>'</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "JSON quotes",
            "id": 120524,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Un oggetto JSON contiene una raccolta di coppie chiave-valore, simile a un oggetto JS.</p><p>Tuttavia, in un JSON dobbiamo racchiudere le chiavi tra virgolette, come <code>\"times\"</code> qui.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" jsonString = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;story&quot;: &quot;Life&quot;, &quot;times&quot;: 2, &quot;fiction&quot;: true }'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"38\" endIndex=\"39\" /><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /><option startIndex=\"39\" endIndex=\"44\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>\"</code>, seguito da <code>times</code> e infine <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Un oggetto JSON contiene una raccolta di coppie chiave-valore, simile a un oggetto JS.</p><p>Le chiavi JSON richiedono virgolette doppie, come <code>\"story\"</code>. Completa la chiave <code>times</code> per il valore <code>2</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" jsonString = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;story&quot;: &quot;Life&quot;, &quot;times&quot;: 2, &quot;fiction&quot;: true }'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"38\" endIndex=\"39\" /><option startIndex=\"39\" endIndex=\"44\" /><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"fiction\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"2\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>\"</code>, seguito da <code>times</code> e infine <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "JSON data types",
            "id": 120525,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Gli oggetti JSON possono raccogliere dati statici come numeri, array, booleani o stringhe. Tuttavia, <strong>non possono</strong> contenere funzioni al loro interno.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" story = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;story&quot;: &quot;Life&quot;,&quot;times&quot;: 2,&quot;fiction&quot;: true}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"58\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"function(){}\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>true</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Gli oggetti JSON possono raccogliere dati statici come numeri, array, booleani o stringhe. Tuttavia, <strong>non possono</strong> contenere funzioni al loro interno.</p><p>Completa la stringa JSON in modo che <code>fiction</code> abbia il valore booleano <code>true</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" story = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;story&quot;: &quot;Life&quot;,&quot;times&quot;: 2,&quot;fiction&quot;: true}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"43\" endIndex=\"52\" /><option startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"58\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"false\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;true&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"function() {}\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>\"fiction\"</code>, seguito da <code>true</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "JSON vs JS object",
            "id": 120526,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Qual è il seguente tipo di dati?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" rainbow = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"colors\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": [\" /><text value=\"&quot;red&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;orange&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;yellow&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;green&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;blue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;purple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"],\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"rain\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Un oggetto JS</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Un JSON</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Un oggetto JS.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Racchiudi tra virgolette singole il valore assegnato a <code>rainbow</code>, senza modificarne il contenuto. È un JSON valido?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" rainbow = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"colors\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": [\" /><text value=\"&quot;red&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;orange&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;yellow&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;green&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;blue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;purple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"],\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"rain\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">No, anche le chiavi richiedono virgolette doppie.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Sì, basta aggiungere le virgolette esterne.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">No, JSON non può contenere array.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">No, anche le chiavi richiedono virgolette doppie.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "JSON Stringify",
            "id": 120527,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Puoi convertire un oggetto JS in JSON con il metodo <code>JSON.stringify()</code>.</p><p>Qui possiamo convertire l'oggetto JS <code>concert</code> in un oggetto JSON se usiamo <code>JSON.stringify(concert)</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" concert = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"band\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"&quot;Super Carrots&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\",\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"music\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"&quot;Indie&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(concert);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".stringify(concert));\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"95\" endIndex=\"99\" /><option startIndex=\"100\" endIndex=\"109\" /><option startIndex=\"110\" endIndex=\"117\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"{ band: 'Super Carrots', music: 'Indie' }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"{&quot;band&quot;:&quot;Super Carrots&quot;,&quot;music&quot;:&quot;Indie&quot;}\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>JSON</code>, seguito da <code>stringify</code> e infine <code>concert</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Puoi convertire un oggetto JS in JSON con il metodo <code>JSON.stringify()</code>.</p><p>Più precisamente, <code>JSON.stringify()</code> restituisce una stringa in formato JSON.</p><p>Converti l'intero oggetto in una stringa JSON per il secondo output della console.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" concert = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"band\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"&quot;Super Carrots&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\",\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"music\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"&quot;Indie&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(concert);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".stringify(concert));\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"95\" endIndex=\"99\" /><option startIndex=\"100\" endIndex=\"109\" /><option startIndex=\"110\" endIndex=\"117\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"parse\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"object\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"music\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"{ band: 'Super Carrots', music: 'Indie' }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"{&quot;band&quot;:&quot;Super Carrots&quot;,&quot;music&quot;:&quot;Indie&quot;}\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>JSON</code>, seguito da <code>stringify</code> e infine <code>concert</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "JSON parse",
            "id": 120528,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Possiamo anche trasformare una stringa JSON in un oggetto JS con il metodo <code>JSON.parse()</code>.</p><p>Se includiamo <code>dog</code> tra parentesi, trasformeremo la stringa JSON in un oggetto JS.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" dog = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Rocko&quot;,&quot;age&quot;:3}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".parse(dog));\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"52\" endIndex=\"56\" /><option startIndex=\"57\" endIndex=\"62\" /><option startIndex=\"63\" endIndex=\"66\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"{ name: 'Rocko', age: 3 }\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>JSON</code>, seguito da <code>parse</code> e infine <code>dog</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Possiamo anche trasformare una stringa JSON in un oggetto JS con il metodo <code>JSON.parse()</code>.</p><p>Converti la stringa JSON memorizzata in un oggetto JS e visualizzalo.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" dog = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Rocko&quot;,&quot;age&quot;:3}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".parse(dog));\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"52\" endIndex=\"56\" /><option startIndex=\"57\" endIndex=\"62\" /><option startIndex=\"63\" endIndex=\"66\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"stringify\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"name\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"age\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"{ name: 'Rocko', age: 3 }\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>JSON</code>, seguito da <code>parse</code> e infine <code>dog</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: json.stringify",
            "id": 120530,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Come possiamo convertire un oggetto JS in una stringa JSON?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Con <code>JSON.stringify</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Con <code>JSON.parse</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Con <code>JSON.stringify</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Hai un oggetto JavaScript e devi inviarne il contenuto come stringa JSON. Quale metodo di conversione esegue questa trasformazione?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Con <code>JSON.stringify</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Con <code>JSON.parse</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Con <code>JSON.object</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere Con <code>JSON.stringify</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Q: JSON.stringify",
            "id": 120531,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Cosa visualizzerà la console?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" birthday = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"attendees\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"13\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"dressCode\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".stringify(birthday));\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"{&quot;attendees&quot;:13,&quot;dressCode&quot;:false}\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>{\"attendees\": 13, \"dressCode\": false}</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>{attendees: 13, dressCode : false}</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>{\"attendees\": 13, \"dressCode\": false}</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Modifichi <code>dressCode</code> in <code>true</code> prima di eseguire il codice. Cosa visualizza ora la console?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" birthday = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"attendees\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"13\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"dressCode\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".stringify(birthday));\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"{&quot;attendees&quot;:13,&quot;dressCode&quot;:false}\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>{\"attendees\":13,\"dressCode\":true}</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>{\"attendees\":13,\"dressCode\":false}</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>{\"attendees\":13,\"dressCode\":\"true\"}</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>{\"attendees\":13,\"dressCode\":true}</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: JSON strings",
            "id": 120532,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Completa il seguente JSON.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" charity = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;name&quot;: &quot;bestHelp&quot;, &quot;donors&quot;: 123 }'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option startIndex=\"23\" endIndex=\"24\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"54\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>'</code>, seguito da <code>\"</code> e poi <code>\"</code>, <code>'</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Completa il seguente JSON. Mantieni l'intero oggetto all'interno di un'unica stringa JavaScript e racchiudi la sua chiave tra virgolette.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" charity = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;name&quot;: &quot;bestHelp&quot;, &quot;donors&quot;: 123 }'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option startIndex=\"23\" endIndex=\"24\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"23\" /><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"27\" /><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"54\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"`\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"donors\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"bestHelp\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>'</code>, seguito da <code>name</code>, <code>\"</code>, <code>\"</code> e infine <code>'</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: JSON.parse",
            "id": 120533,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>*<em>Analizza</em> la stringa JSON <code>brochure</code> in modo da visualizzare un oggetto JS nell'output della console.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" brochure = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;title&quot;: &quot;Summer Vacation&quot;, &quot;destination&quot;:&quot;France&quot;}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" parsedBrochure = \" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".parse(brochure);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(parsedBrochure);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"101\" endIndex=\"106\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"{ title: 'Summer Vacation', destination: 'France' }\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di digitare <code>parse</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
